---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Apryse WebViewer: PDF Viewer & Editor"
  description="Apryse WebViewer is a JavaScript PDF viewer and editor for viewing and annotating PDFs, Office documents and images in any web app. Andrey Safonov was its product manager."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Portfolio', path: '/portfolio' }, { name: 'WebViewer', path: '/portfolio/webviewer-product' }]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pt-14 sm:px-6">
    <p class="mb-3 text-sm font-medium text-accent">Portfolio · Apryse</p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">PDF Viewer & Editor (WebViewer)</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      WebViewer is an embeddable PDF viewer and editor for any web application. It lets startups and enterprises build document
      workflows without users downloading files and editing them somewhere else. It is used by Dropbox, DocuSign, Microsoft, Smallpdf and thousands more,
      with 100K weekly downloads. As the first product manager, I worked with two development teams to modernize the UI, expand the feature set,
      reduce technical debt and add support for more file formats.
    </p>
    <img src="/cases/webviewer.png" alt="WebViewer screenshot" class="mt-8 w-full rounded-2xl border border-line" />
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="https://showcase.apryse.com/" class="rounded-lg bg-accent px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-accent-ink">Try the live demo on Apryse ↗</a>
      <a href="https://apryse.com/blog/webviewer/create-easy-custom-signature-workflows" class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium">Digital signatures launch ↗</a>
      <a href="/portfolio" class="rounded-lg px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-muted">← Back to portfolio</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
